# This file used to hold a "Medieval Baghdad" example in a private whg: vocabulary
# (http://whgazetteer.org/ontology/). It has been withdrawn, not ported: WHG's RDF is
# PLATO RDF (https://w3id.org/plato#), and the example's sources, contributors, dates and
# coordinates were illustrative rather than taken from the works it named, so a PLATO
# version would have presented invented claims as attested ones.
#
# For worked examples in PLATO RDF, use PLATO's own files:
#   https://github.com/pelagios/place-attestation-ontology/tree/main/examples
#   constantinople.ttl        one place, three attestations (names, geometries, timespans, a type)
#   antonine-routes.ttl       a route, its stations and segments
#   king-john-itinerary.ttl   an itinerary, dated stop by stop, with a denial
#   river-idle-network.ttl    a physical network
#   datini-network.ttl        a relational network with figures on its links
#
# See ../rdf-representation.md for how WHG uses them.
